        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The central artifacts in Spring’s Java configuration support are "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Configuration"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "-annotated classes and "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Bean"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "-annotated methods."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Bean"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " annotation is used to indicate that a method instantiates, configures, and initializes a new object to be managed by the Spring IoC container. For those familiar with Spring’s "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "<beans/>"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " XML configuration, the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Bean"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " annotation plays the same role as the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "<bean/>"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " element. You can use "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Bean"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "-annotated methods with any Spring "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Component"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ". However, they are most often used with "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Configuration"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " beans."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Annotating a class with "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Configuration"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " indicates that its primary purpose is as a source of bean definitions. Furthermore, "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Configuration"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " classes let inter-bean dependencies be defined by calling other "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Bean"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " methods in the same class. The simplest possible "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Configuration"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " class reads as follows:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "dlist",
            "id": null,
            "items": [
              {
                "description": {
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "context": "listing",
                      "id": null,
                      "inlines": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "@Configuration\npublic class AppConfig {\n\n\t@Bean\n\tpublic MyServiceImpl myService() {\n\t\treturn new MyServiceImpl();\n\t}\n}"
                        }
                      ],
                      "language": "java",
                      "roles": [],
                      "title": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "checkbox": null,
                  "inlines": []
                },
                "terms": [
                  [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": "Java"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              },
              {
                "description": {
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "context": "listing",
                      "id": null,
                      "inlines": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "@Configuration\nclass AppConfig {\n\n\t@Bean\n\tfun myService(): MyServiceImpl {\n\t\treturn MyServiceImpl()\n\t}\n}"
                        }
                      ],
                      "language": "kotlin",
                      "roles": [],
                      "title": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "checkbox": null,
                  "inlines": []
                },
                "terms": [
                  [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": "Kotlin"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "example",
        "id": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The preceding "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "AppConfig"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " class is equivalent to the following Spring "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "<beans/>"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " XML:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "listing",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "<beans>\n\t<bean id=\"myService\" class=\"com.acme.services.MyServiceImpl\"/>\n</beans>"
          }
        ],
        "language": "xml",
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "In common scenarios, "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@Bean"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " methods are to be declared within "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@Configuration"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " classes, ensuring that full configuration class processing applies and that cross-method references therefore get redirected to the container’s lifecycle management. This prevents the same "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@Bean"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " method from accidentally being invoked through a regular Java method call, which helps to reduce subtle bugs that can be hard to track down."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "When "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@Bean"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " methods are declared within classes that are not annotated with "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@Configuration"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " - or when "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@Configuration(proxyBeanMethods=false)"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " is declared -, they are referred to as being processed in a \"lite\" mode. In such scenarios, "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@Bean"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " methods are effectively a general-purpose factory method mechanism without special runtime processing (that is, without generating a CGLIB subclass for it). A custom Java call to such a method will not get intercepted by the container and therefore behaves just like a regular method call, creating a new instance every time rather than reusing an existing singleton (or scoped) instance for the given bean."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "As a consequence, "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@Bean"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " methods on classes without runtime proxying are not meant to declare inter-bean dependencies at all. Instead, they are expected to operate on their containing component’s fields and, optionally, on arguments that a factory method may declare in order to receive autowired collaborators. Such a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@Bean"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " method therefore never needs to invoke other "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@Bean"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " methods; every such call can be expressed through a factory method argument instead. The positive side-effect here is that no CGLIB subclassing has to be applied at runtime, reducing the overhead and the footprint."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "sidebar",
        "id": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "@Configuration classes with or without local calls between @Bean methods?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Bean"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " and "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Configuration"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " annotations are discussed in depth in the following sections. First, however, we cover the various ways of creating a Spring container by using Java-based configuration."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      }
    ],
